# VS Code REST Client syntax. The client extension is optional; any HTTP client can send these requests.
# ADAPTER_ACCESS_TOKEN must be a USER access token for the adapter API, never an ID token or a Power Platform token.
# Keep it in your local environment, not in this file. REST Client may need an editor restart to see new environment variables.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5180
@agent = support

### Health (local readiness only, no downstream message)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Configured agents, without their secret connection URLs
GET {{baseUrl}}/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{$processEnv ADAPTER_ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Discover this agent
GET {{baseUrl}}/copilot-studio/{{agent}}/a2a/.well-known/agent-card.json

### End-to-end connection test: adapter -> delegated OBO -> Copilot Studio -> A2A text reply
# @name firstTurn
POST {{baseUrl}}/copilot-studio/{{agent}}/a2a
Authorization: Bearer {{$processEnv ADAPTER_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json
A2A-Version: 1.0

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "{{$guid}}",
  "method": "SendMessage",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
      "role": "ROLE_USER",
      "parts": [{ "text": "Reply with a short greeting.", "mediaType": "text/plain" }]
    },
    "configuration": { "acceptedOutputModes": ["text/plain"], "returnImmediately": false }
  }
}

### Continue the context returned by firstTurn (send firstTurn successfully first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/copilot-studio/{{agent}}/a2a
Authorization: Bearer {{$processEnv ADAPTER_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json
A2A-Version: 1.0

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "{{$guid}}",
  "method": "SendMessage",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "messageId": "{{$guid}}",
      "contextId": "{{firstTurn.response.body.$.result.message.contextId}}",
      "role": "ROLE_USER",
      "parts": [{ "text": "What was my previous message?" }]
    }
  }
}